  "starterCode": "# Grouped Query Attention \u2014 reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(q, k, v, causal=False):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### \ud83d\udca1 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Grouped Query Attention** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### \u26a1 Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(q, k, v, causal=False):\n    q=np.asarray(q,dtype=float); k=np.asarray(k,dtype=float); v=np.asarray(v,dtype=float)\n    # Inputs are [heads, sequence, head_dim]; K/V heads are repeated to query-head count.\n    h=q.shape[0]\n    if h % k.shape[0]: raise ValueError(\"query heads must be divisible by KV heads\")\n    k=np.repeat(k,h//k.shape[0],axis=0); v=np.repeat(v,h//v.shape[0],axis=0)\n    scores=q@np.swapaxes(k,-1,-2)/np.sqrt(q.shape[-1])\n    if causal:\n        mask=np.triu(np.ones(scores.shape[-2:],dtype=bool),k=1)\n        scores=np.where(mask,-1e30,scores)\n    e=np.exp(scores-scores.max(axis=-1,keepdims=True)); p=e/e.sum(axis=-1,keepdims=True)\n    return (p@v).tolist()\n```\n\n### \u23f1\ufe0f Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
